1
00:00:00,365 --> 00:00:01,425
9 weeks ago,

2
00:00:01,435 --> 00:00:05,675
I decided to commit to the hardest
physical challenge of my whole life:

3
00:00:05,685 --> 00:00:07,396
running a marathon.

4
00:00:07,406 --> 00:00:09,309
This is going to be a tough one.

5
00:00:09,319 --> 00:00:11,706
My legs are burning like hell.

6
00:00:11,716 --> 00:00:14,358
It f*cking rains. I f*cking knew it.

7
00:00:24,873 --> 00:00:26,013
Oh my God.

8
00:00:28,586 --> 00:00:29,792
No excuses!

9
00:00:30,501 --> 00:00:32,686
My calf is just hurting so much.

10
00:00:33,524 --> 00:00:35,784
I'm actually doubting myself right now

11
00:00:35,794 --> 00:00:38,266
if I will be able to run 42 kilometers,

12
00:00:38,276 --> 00:00:41,352
or if this goal was just way too huge for me.

13
00:00:50,157 --> 00:00:52,077
Alright, let's give you some context here.

14
00:00:52,087 --> 00:00:53,445
I used to hate running,

15
00:00:53,455 --> 00:00:57,105
up until the point when three years ago
I signed up for a half marathon.

16
00:00:57,115 --> 00:00:59,369
I started to go for runs a few times per week

17
00:00:59,379 --> 00:01:03,075
and fell in love with the physical and mental
challenges that come with it.

18
00:01:03,085 --> 00:01:05,805
I finished my half marathon
in 1 hour and 34 minutes

19
00:01:05,815 --> 00:01:08,711
and told myself that one day I
would run a full marathon.

20
00:01:08,721 --> 00:01:13,126
I quickly found out that I had massively
underestimated how much more challenging it is

21
00:01:13,136 --> 00:01:15,777
to run 42 kilometers instead of 21,

22
00:01:15,787 --> 00:01:18,559
so I dropped the idea and forgot about it.

23
00:01:18,569 --> 00:01:21,429
But 9 weeks ago, when I decided
to move to South Africa,

24
00:01:21,439 --> 00:01:25,507
I saw that there was a marathon taking place
on the 17th of October in Cape Town,

25
00:01:25,517 --> 00:01:28,232
and that's when I knew that
the time had finally come

26
00:01:28,242 --> 00:01:31,291
to once and for all face this huge challenge.

27
00:01:31,301 --> 00:01:35,109
I already jumped into my laptop
and looked for some articles

28
00:01:35,119 --> 00:01:37,755
on how to properly train for a marathon,

29
00:01:37,765 --> 00:01:39,624
and as it turns out,

30
00:01:39,634 --> 00:01:43,772
a lot of these articles say that you have
to train at least for 4 months.

31
00:01:43,782 --> 00:01:48,503
I just realized that I have
a total of nine weeks to pull this off,

32
00:01:48,513 --> 00:01:49,860
which is a bummer.

33
00:01:50,317 --> 00:01:51,483
And I'm scared.

34
00:01:51,908 --> 00:01:54,889
As I said, I have a total of 9 weeks to train.

35
00:01:54,899 --> 00:01:58,064
Throughout the whole training, I
will do three different types of runs.

36
00:01:58,074 --> 00:01:59,760
Easy ones for my weekly mileage,

37
00:01:59,770 --> 00:02:01,309
long rounds for my endurance,

38
00:02:01,319 --> 00:02:03,335
and interval runs for my speed work.

39
00:02:03,345 --> 00:02:07,462
In between those runs, I have days to rest
my muscles and recharge for the next one.

40
00:02:07,472 --> 00:02:12,167
The plan is to slowly increase the easy runs
from 8 kilometers up to 13 kilometers.

41
00:02:12,177 --> 00:02:16,720
Around every 8 days, I have my long runs
which will start at 18 kilometers,

42
00:02:16,730 --> 00:02:20,070
and step up to the longest run with 33 kilometers.

43
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:23,896
In week 8 I will lower the distance,
and in week 9 I rest completely,

44
00:02:23,906 --> 00:02:26,598
in order to be fully recharged for the marathon.

45
00:02:26,608 --> 00:02:30,508
All of this combined would bring us
to a total of 29 runs

46
00:02:30,518 --> 00:02:33,077
and 409 kilometers.

47
00:02:33,087 --> 00:02:36,949
I'm hoping that this training plan is achievable.

48
00:02:36,959 --> 00:02:39,402
I think now I just gotta get started.

49
00:02:39,412 --> 00:02:40,563
Let's do it.

50
00:02:42,239 --> 00:02:43,843
So, it is pouring rain

51
00:02:43,853 --> 00:02:47,004
and I'm about to get myself
some new running shoes.

52
00:02:48,553 --> 00:02:49,677
Running shoes.

53
00:02:49,687 --> 00:02:51,247
They're like the horse of a rider,

54
00:02:51,257 --> 00:02:54,398
the bike of a cyclist, or the car
of a racing driver.

55
00:02:54,408 --> 00:02:57,708
The shoes are the only thing that separates
the runner from the ground,

56
00:02:57,718 --> 00:03:01,491
and it is super important to find
the perfect pair for your needs.

57
00:03:04,607 --> 00:03:06,762
So many shoes.

58
00:03:06,772 --> 00:03:09,918
We analyzed my foot posture,
I tried one pair after another

59
00:03:09,928 --> 00:03:12,845
and ran through the whole store
in order to test them out.

60
00:03:14,933 --> 00:03:18,393
The crazy thing is that all of these shoes
actually feel completely different,

61
00:03:18,403 --> 00:03:21,125
like one is softer, the other one fits better.

62
00:03:21,135 --> 00:03:23,578
It's driving different kinds of cars, actually.

63
00:03:23,588 --> 00:03:24,776
I found the ones.

64
00:03:26,643 --> 00:03:27,593
Let's go!

65
00:03:28,056 --> 00:03:31,288
Next up, I had to buy a proper
tracking device for my runs.

66
00:03:31,298 --> 00:03:32,233
Hey.

67
00:03:32,846 --> 00:03:34,208
I wanna buy your Apple Watch.

68
00:03:34,218 --> 00:03:35,333
A little bit more.

69
00:03:37,306 --> 00:03:40,661
So, my brother already gave up
on his running ambitions,

70
00:03:40,671 --> 00:03:43,750
so that's why he decided to sell me
his Apple Watch, right?

71
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,119
Definitely not true.

72
00:03:45,862 --> 00:03:49,012
He actually already did a marathon,
but which time did you run?

73
00:03:49,022 --> 00:03:50,476
3 hours 41.

74
00:03:50,486 --> 00:03:52,693
3 hours 41? I think that is pretty good.

75
00:03:52,703 --> 00:03:55,229
I'm curious if I'm gonna beat it.
What do you think?

76
00:03:55,239 --> 00:03:57,191
Well, not if you start training two months before.

77
00:03:57,201 --> 00:03:59,047
How long before did you start training?

78
00:03:59,683 --> 00:04:00,606
Also.

79
00:04:01,179 --> 00:04:02,537
Roughly two months.

80
00:04:03,099 --> 00:04:07,211
So, after buying my brother's Apple Watch and
being equipped with some proper running shoes,

81
00:04:07,221 --> 00:04:09,979
I was finally ready to hit the road.

82
00:04:44,779 --> 00:04:49,328
The first runs were pretty easy, as I was super
motivated to get this whole thing started.

83
00:04:49,338 --> 00:04:51,679
Second run going well so far.

84
00:04:51,689 --> 00:04:52,984
Shoes are feeling good.

85
00:04:52,994 --> 00:04:55,519
After a long period of barely doing any sports,

86
00:04:55,529 --> 00:04:59,374
it felt really good to move my body again
and see some sunlight.

87
00:05:02,137 --> 00:05:05,198
My usual running procedure was
around 5 minutes of warming up

88
00:05:05,208 --> 00:05:07,353
by doing a couple of different exercises.

89
00:05:07,363 --> 00:05:10,542
Then I would make my way from the city
into the nearby English Garden,

90
00:05:10,552 --> 00:05:12,630
which is the biggest park in Munich.

91
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:17,171
It's a beautiful piece of nature and
the perfect environment to go for a run.

92
00:05:17,181 --> 00:05:20,699
No traffic, no red lights,
only trees and fresh air.

93
00:05:20,709 --> 00:05:23,678
After the runs, I tried to stretch myself
for a couple of minutes,

94
00:05:23,688 --> 00:05:28,383
but it occasionally happened that
I got hungry and a little bit distracted.

95
00:05:28,393 --> 00:05:30,409
That one is well deserved.

96
00:05:31,788 --> 00:05:36,716
After taking off my first three easy runs,
it was time for the first long run.

97
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,315
No excuses!

98
00:05:40,912 --> 00:05:42,486
It's raining so hard.

99
00:05:45,768 --> 00:05:48,768
Oh my God, the rain just doesn't stop, hey.

100
00:05:59,268 --> 00:06:00,768
Holy sh*t, so...

101
00:06:00,778 --> 00:06:02,658
I  just ran 19 kilometers,

102
00:06:02,668 --> 00:06:04,497
I can definitely feel my legs.

103
00:06:04,507 --> 00:06:07,438
I think in total I did like
50 kilometers this week,

104
00:06:07,448 --> 00:06:11,709
and now I can really feel the muscles
getting sore right now.

105
00:06:11,719 --> 00:06:14,460
I'm definitely gonna feel that
tomorrow morning, hey.

106
00:06:20,855 --> 00:06:23,223
Like, doing this 19 kilometers run today

107
00:06:23,233 --> 00:06:27,605
really showed me like how
freaking long a marathon is.

108
00:06:27,615 --> 00:06:31,351
Like, I have to run more than
twice as much as today,

109
00:06:31,361 --> 00:06:34,062
and my legs are already like jello.

110
00:06:34,072 --> 00:06:39,115
I don't really know how to do it in
eight weeks or in seven weeks,

111
00:06:39,513 --> 00:06:42,198
but I hope I'm gonna be fine.

112
00:06:44,767 --> 00:06:47,522
In week two, I headed out
together with my friend Nico,

113
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:50,468
which was a nice change from running by myself.

114
00:06:51,351 --> 00:06:54,135
As the days passed, I made
some more steady progress

115
00:06:54,145 --> 00:06:57,859
by ticking off my first interval run
and two more easy runs.

116
00:06:59,390 --> 00:07:01,882
So, it's the beginning of the third week,

117
00:07:01,892 --> 00:07:06,765
which means today I have my second
long run of 21 kilometers.

118
00:07:06,775 --> 00:07:10,959
I tried to postpone it all day long because
it was raining all the time. Like,

119
00:07:10,969 --> 00:07:15,185
outside here in Germany the weather
is so bad, but yeah...

120
00:07:15,749 --> 00:07:17,721
It stopped raining, so...

121
00:07:17,903 --> 00:07:19,848
I guess I have to run. F*ck.

122
00:07:29,174 --> 00:07:31,014
This is going to be a long run, hey.

123
00:07:31,024 --> 00:07:32,970
I just hope it doesn't rain.

124
00:07:40,959 --> 00:07:45,798
By running along the different rivers, I could see
how much it actually rained in the last days.

125
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:48,467
The whole city is literally flooded.

126
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,848
Guess what? It f*cking rains.

127
00:07:57,858 --> 00:07:59,489
I f*cking knew it!

128
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:01,793
What is this?

129
00:08:01,803 --> 00:08:04,137
There are puddles everywhere,
you can't really run at all.

130
00:08:04,147 --> 00:08:05,257
This is sh*t.

131
00:08:06,964 --> 00:08:09,268
Are you f*cking serious?

132
00:08:09,278 --> 00:08:12,689
I don't really know how I'm still
going to make 13 kilometers,

133
00:08:12,699 --> 00:08:15,732
because as you see, there are
f*cking huge puddles everywhere.

134
00:08:15,742 --> 00:08:17,671
Holy sh*t, this is crazy.

135
00:08:17,681 --> 00:08:21,267
The rain was so strong that I actually
wanted to return back home.

136
00:08:21,277 --> 00:08:23,051
There's no use in running like that.

137
00:08:23,061 --> 00:08:25,421
But as I didn't want to cancel
my second long run,

138
00:08:25,431 --> 00:08:28,736
I decided to keep up the spirit and push through.

139
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:30,360
High five?

140
00:08:30,370 --> 00:08:31,338
No?

141
00:08:47,295 --> 00:08:51,312
This was definitely the worst run
I ever had in my whole life.

142
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:55,771
When it comes to the conditions for the last one
hour or last one and a half hours actually,

143
00:08:55,781 --> 00:08:57,727
I was just running in the pouring rain.

144
00:08:57,737 --> 00:09:01,232
I'm glad I pulled through.
I did the full 21 kilometers.

145
00:09:02,093 --> 00:09:05,955
Why do my long runs always need
to be when it's freaking raining?

146
00:09:06,867 --> 00:09:08,243
I don't get it.

147
00:09:09,237 --> 00:09:11,701
I was able to check off every run that week,

148
00:09:11,711 --> 00:09:15,513
but during my last one, I started
to feel some pain in my leg

149
00:09:15,523 --> 00:09:17,620
and had to cut the run short.

150
00:09:17,630 --> 00:09:21,985
I developed a little bit of pain in my left knee
and also in my achilles tendon.

151
00:09:21,995 --> 00:09:25,851
That kind of sucks, but I just
feel like I shouldn't run

152
00:09:25,861 --> 00:09:27,757
if I'm slowly developing pain,

153
00:09:27,767 --> 00:09:30,880
because if I just keep running,
it just gets worse and worse,

154
00:09:30,890 --> 00:09:33,724
and then you can't get out of it
and the marathon is done.

155
00:09:34,039 --> 00:09:36,243
I just hope that it doesn't get worse.

156
00:09:41,763 --> 00:09:44,415
Hello and welcome to my yoga class!

157
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:53,247
Okay, cut the bullsh*t.

158
00:09:53,257 --> 00:09:56,033
The fact alone that I call it a yoga class

159
00:09:56,043 --> 00:09:58,579
shows you how much I know about stretching.

160
00:09:58,589 --> 00:10:02,600
So, these things have been laying around
in the corner of my room

161
00:10:02,610 --> 00:10:04,275
for the last 2 and a half weeks.

162
00:10:04,285 --> 00:10:06,821
I didn't use them once, even though I wanted to.

163
00:10:06,831 --> 00:10:10,303
I'm just a lazy f*ck when it comes to stretching,

164
00:10:10,313 --> 00:10:12,800
because I always think that
it doesn't have any impact

165
00:10:12,810 --> 00:10:15,236
on getting better when it comes to the marathon,

166
00:10:15,246 --> 00:10:17,634
but I think I should really do more of it,

167
00:10:17,644 --> 00:10:20,922
because I actually had a call with
a physiotherapist earlier today,

168
00:10:20,932 --> 00:10:25,381
and I asked her what I could do
in order to prevent pain in my knees,

169
00:10:25,391 --> 00:10:27,585
because that is my main concern
when it comes to running.

170
00:10:27,595 --> 00:10:29,783
She actually told me two things.

171
00:10:29,793 --> 00:10:31,573
First, I should stretch more,

172
00:10:31,583 --> 00:10:34,000
and the second part is muscle training.

173
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:37,802
Just running is not enough in order to
make it for the marathon,

174
00:10:37,812 --> 00:10:41,830
so that's why I gotta adjust and
that's why I gotta do some extra stuff.

175
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:43,381
Let's see how that turns out.

176
00:10:43,391 --> 00:10:45,218
As I do it with everything,

177
00:10:45,228 --> 00:10:46,989
I asked YouTube for advice

178
00:10:46,999 --> 00:10:51,149
and tried to match the different exercises
which were shown in the video.

179
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:01,907
This feels good.

180
00:11:02,504 --> 00:11:04,841
While I quickly got hold of the normal stretches,

181
00:11:04,851 --> 00:11:07,742
the foam roll was a whole new level.

182
00:11:12,018 --> 00:11:13,742
Honestly, I would rather run

183
00:11:13,752 --> 00:11:16,818
for 40 kilometers than doing this all the time.

184
00:11:22,793 --> 00:11:24,426
I hope that this helps, hey.

185
00:11:24,436 --> 00:11:28,283
After 30 minutes of pain, I could actually notice
how my muscles loosened up,

186
00:11:28,293 --> 00:11:30,702
and it felt like I relieved some tension.

187
00:11:32,441 --> 00:11:37,013
On the next day, I got started with the muscle
training by doing some bodyweight exercices.

188
00:11:37,023 --> 00:11:40,057
With those exercises, I was
definitely more experienced,

189
00:11:40,067 --> 00:11:43,880
but a few days later,
the consequences started to show.

190
00:11:49,786 --> 00:11:54,347
I just put the foot of the chair on my toes.

191
00:11:56,193 --> 00:12:00,363
The upper leg on my right side is so sore.

192
00:12:00,373 --> 00:12:01,815
I can barely walk.

193
00:12:01,825 --> 00:12:04,191
Like, I'm just running around like a grandpa.

194
00:12:04,201 --> 00:12:09,272
It just sucks, because actually yesterday I
wanted to do my third long run of 24 kilometers,

195
00:12:09,282 --> 00:12:11,123
but I just couldn't really walk.

196
00:12:11,133 --> 00:12:13,892
Like, I actually struggled putting on my socks.

197
00:12:13,902 --> 00:12:17,481
It's really bad to be honest, because I
just wanted to stick to my training plan,

198
00:12:17,491 --> 00:12:21,080
and now I have to skip it for one day,
probably I have to skip it for another day.

199
00:12:21,090 --> 00:12:22,075
Yeah.

200
00:12:22,406 --> 00:12:24,581
I should have trained more legs back then.

201
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:32,440
My muscles are still sore,

202
00:12:32,450 --> 00:12:35,188
but today I gotta do my long run.

203
00:12:35,198 --> 00:12:37,978
Not really feeling like it,
feeling a little bit tired,

204
00:12:37,988 --> 00:12:39,590
feeling a little bit exhausted,

205
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:42,210
but I gotta do it. I gotta do it today.

206
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:46,870
I didn't really feel like running 24k at
all and after the first few minutes,

207
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:49,497
I could already feel my legs getting weak.

208
00:12:50,093 --> 00:12:52,480
This is going to be a tough one, hey.

209
00:12:53,243 --> 00:12:56,093
But still, I was determined to get this run done.

210
00:12:56,103 --> 00:12:58,473
A few years ago, I simply couldn't understand

211
00:12:58,483 --> 00:13:01,993
why anybody would voluntarily
run for such a long distance.

212
00:13:02,003 --> 00:13:05,192
It's exhausting, time consuming and monotonous.

213
00:13:05,202 --> 00:13:07,373
Why would anybody find pleasure in that?

214
00:13:07,383 --> 00:13:10,363
In the world of running, there is something
called a "runner's high",

215
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:14,805
which is described as a brief,
deeply relaxing state of euphoria.

216
00:13:14,815 --> 00:13:16,522
When running for long distances,

217
00:13:16,532 --> 00:13:20,219
it often happens that you get lost in
that monotonous motion.

218
00:13:21,313 --> 00:13:23,484
Foot after foot, breath after breath,

219
00:13:23,494 --> 00:13:27,655
your mind is so busy focusing on that
repetitive motion of your body

220
00:13:27,665 --> 00:13:30,330
that everything around you starts to slow down

221
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:32,319
and you enter a meditative state.

222
00:13:32,329 --> 00:13:37,088
You feel the wind blowing along your face
and you watch your legs move on autopilot.

223
00:13:37,098 --> 00:13:38,958
It's just you in your tunnel,

224
00:13:38,968 --> 00:13:41,274
no distractions, no stress.

225
00:13:41,284 --> 00:13:44,641
A place where your thoughts are clear
and your mind can run free.

226
00:13:44,651 --> 00:13:47,731
During my long runs, I experienced
these moments all the time,

227
00:13:47,741 --> 00:13:51,439
and I really felt like it had an incredible
impact on my mental health.

228
00:13:51,449 --> 00:13:53,352
Also during my 24k run,

229
00:13:53,362 --> 00:13:55,872
the runner's high was what
helped me push through.

230
00:13:55,882 --> 00:13:57,983
I gotta say it's feeling better,

231
00:13:57,993 --> 00:14:00,560
because as soon as you're in a flow
and you're just running,

232
00:14:00,570 --> 00:14:02,556
you kind of forget about your legs.

233
00:14:02,566 --> 00:14:07,843
But as soon as I stop to film, then I
just really feel the legs creeping back in.

234
00:14:07,853 --> 00:14:10,398
At least the weather is good today.

235
00:14:10,408 --> 00:14:13,306
24 f*cking kilometers.

236
00:14:13,316 --> 00:14:16,340
My legs are burning, and I think
I'm just going to jump into the river

237
00:14:16,350 --> 00:14:18,246
in order to cool down here.

238
00:14:25,108 --> 00:14:26,915
That feels so good.

239
00:14:28,605 --> 00:14:31,141
I'm actually really happy that
I pulled through with this run.

240
00:14:31,151 --> 00:14:34,905
In the beginning, I really didn't think that
I would make more than 10 kilometers.

241
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:36,612
This gives some more confidence again

242
00:14:36,622 --> 00:14:38,816
that I actually make the marathon.

243
00:14:38,826 --> 00:14:41,319
Look at all the ducks hanging out with me.

244
00:14:44,021 --> 00:14:46,513
I was now almost halfway through my training,

245
00:14:46,523 --> 00:14:50,309
and I knew that these next four weeks
would be the most important ones

246
00:14:50,319 --> 00:14:52,457
to prepare my body for the marathon.

247
00:14:56,418 --> 00:14:59,134
Even though my energy was drained
from the weeks before,

248
00:14:59,144 --> 00:15:01,720
I dedicated myself and stuck to the plan.

249
00:15:01,730 --> 00:15:06,506
My easy runs now had a distance of 11 kilometers
and they felt better from time to time.

250
00:15:06,516 --> 00:15:10,171
I could feel how my muscles and my endurance
were improving with each run,

251
00:15:10,181 --> 00:15:13,194
and those distances now felt
like a short jog to me.

252
00:15:13,204 --> 00:15:15,754
In week 5, I checked off another interval run.

253
00:15:15,764 --> 00:15:19,814
Those high speed runs helped me strengthen
my muscles and increase my pace.

254
00:15:19,824 --> 00:15:21,721
I started to enjoy running more and more,

255
00:15:21,731 --> 00:15:24,559
and it quickly became my favorite part of the day.

256
00:15:24,569 --> 00:15:26,643
It felt like instead of draining my energy,

257
00:15:26,653 --> 00:15:29,385
it now actually started to fuel my vitality,

258
00:15:29,395 --> 00:15:33,346
and seeing the marathon move closer
got me motivated even more.

259
00:15:33,356 --> 00:15:37,813
I headed out during any time of the day
and pushed my body to perform at its peak.

260
00:15:37,823 --> 00:15:41,227
Sunrise, midday, sunset, midnight.

261
00:15:41,237 --> 00:15:46,475
With each run, I could feel my body evolving and
I pushed my limits to distances and paces

262
00:15:46,485 --> 00:15:48,762
which before seemed completely out of reach.

263
00:15:48,772 --> 00:15:52,401
I was at an all-time high and
checked off one run after another.

264
00:15:52,411 --> 00:15:54,799
My muscles are just getting more and more stable.

265
00:15:54,809 --> 00:15:58,645
I'm definitely improving, I really feel like
my body is kind of like evolving.

266
00:16:01,385 --> 00:16:05,921
With my fourth long run, I approach distances
where I would need to refuel my body,

267
00:16:05,931 --> 00:16:07,904
so I bought myself some POWERGELs,

268
00:16:07,914 --> 00:16:10,439
which contain a lot of carbohydrates and sugar.

269
00:16:10,449 --> 00:16:12,312
I mean, a lot of sugar.

270
00:16:14,069 --> 00:16:15,959
Oh my God, this is so sweet.

271
00:16:15,969 --> 00:16:18,879
Mango, passion fruit,
this is just like pure sugar.

272
00:16:18,889 --> 00:16:21,743
I sticked one of them into my back pocket
in order to have a booster

273
00:16:21,753 --> 00:16:23,732
when my energy would start to decrease.

274
00:16:23,742 --> 00:16:27,767
The 27 kilometer-long run was probably
one of my all-time favourites,

275
00:16:27,777 --> 00:16:29,749
as I finally had some good weather.

276
00:16:29,759 --> 00:16:31,197
Finally a sunny long run.

277
00:16:31,207 --> 00:16:34,305
And discovered some of the most
beautiful spots in my city.

278
00:16:34,315 --> 00:16:37,487
Honestly, how beautiful is this place?

279
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:40,172
I'm seeing so many new corners of Munich

280
00:16:40,182 --> 00:16:41,770
now that I'm running so long.

281
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:44,929
While my booster definitely
provided some extra energy,

282
00:16:44,939 --> 00:16:48,810
this distance was something my legs
were definitely not used to.

283
00:16:50,534 --> 00:16:51,916
Oh my God.

284
00:16:51,926 --> 00:16:54,437
Holy sh*t, was that exhausting.

285
00:16:59,739 --> 00:17:03,016
Like after you do these long runs and
then like 5 minutes after you stop,

286
00:17:03,026 --> 00:17:06,078
it just really creeps into your muscles

287
00:17:06,088 --> 00:17:07,860
and you almost can't walk.

288
00:17:07,870 --> 00:17:10,190
That's why it's so important
to stretch after a run,

289
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:12,948
even though I don't feel like
stretching at all right now.

290
00:17:12,958 --> 00:17:14,155
I gotta do it.

291
00:17:18,939 --> 00:17:22,629
It feels like I'm almost getting
a cramp in my muscles.

292
00:17:22,639 --> 00:17:23,594
Whoa.

293
00:17:29,703 --> 00:17:30,624
F*ck.

294
00:17:30,634 --> 00:17:31,710
Sh*t.

295
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:34,823
Alright, that's enough of moaning for you today.

296
00:17:35,185 --> 00:17:36,754
It really is that bad.

297
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,513
None of the sh*t is acted.

298
00:17:38,523 --> 00:17:40,065
I'm f*cking dying.

299
00:17:41,065 --> 00:17:42,565
Okay, that is not true.

300
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:46,948
We are now in week six.

301
00:17:46,958 --> 00:17:50,331
I still have like two to three weeks to go
when it comes to the training.

302
00:17:50,341 --> 00:17:53,917
It's going well, but I feel like I'm just
getting a little bit too comfortable now,

303
00:17:53,927 --> 00:17:57,762
because this week should have been actually
the week where I run the longest distance.

304
00:17:57,772 --> 00:18:01,251
Two days ago, I ran 9 kilometers instead of 13,

305
00:18:01,261 --> 00:18:03,793
so I'm cutting shorter than I usually should.

306
00:18:03,803 --> 00:18:06,055
And also, I'm going to leave to
Vienna on the weekend

307
00:18:06,065 --> 00:18:08,414
to meet with 3 of my friends
and go partying a little bit,

308
00:18:08,424 --> 00:18:12,107
so that's not beneficial at all and
I can't do any runs during that time.

309
00:18:12,117 --> 00:18:15,304
So yeah, I feel like I'm really just
lacking the discipline

310
00:18:15,314 --> 00:18:17,484
to kind of like pull through right now.

311
00:18:17,494 --> 00:18:20,356
But I have an idea in order to fix that.

312
00:18:22,697 --> 00:18:26,384
Actually, I didn't book my tickets so far, because
I wasn't sure if my buddy was going to hold up,

313
00:18:26,394 --> 00:18:28,060
but now that I'm more confident,

314
00:18:28,070 --> 00:18:32,159
I think I'm just going to lock it in
because then there is no way back.

315
00:18:32,169 --> 00:18:34,138
Sanlam Cape Town marathon.

316
00:18:34,148 --> 00:18:35,682
October 17th.

317
00:18:35,692 --> 00:18:38,137
42.2 kilometers.

318
00:18:40,282 --> 00:18:41,218
Enter.

319
00:18:41,421 --> 00:18:42,569
Buy an entry.

320
00:18:42,579 --> 00:18:43,725
Marathon...

321
00:18:44,211 --> 00:18:45,614
Sold out? No!

322
00:18:45,923 --> 00:18:47,115
Are you kidding me?

323
00:18:47,125 --> 00:18:48,430
No way.

324
00:18:48,739 --> 00:18:50,787
The whole marathon is sold out.

325
00:18:51,131 --> 00:18:52,558
No...

326
00:18:53,788 --> 00:18:54,661
F*ck.

327
00:18:54,671 --> 00:18:56,886
That is so freaking unfortunate.

328
00:18:56,896 --> 00:18:58,326
Damn, I really...

329
00:18:58,336 --> 00:19:00,311
don't know what I'm gonna do now.

330
00:19:00,321 --> 00:19:03,736
I missed the deadline of the marathon by one day,

331
00:19:03,746 --> 00:19:05,802
and now all entries were closed.

332
00:19:05,812 --> 00:19:10,034
All the motivation that I built up over the last
weeks was gone with the blink of an eye,

333
00:19:10,044 --> 00:19:12,551
as I had no more goal to work towards to.

334
00:19:12,561 --> 00:19:14,913
I decided to write an email
to the racing committee

335
00:19:14,923 --> 00:19:17,837
with a request to still issue
a marathon ticket for me.

336
00:19:17,847 --> 00:19:20,208
Now all I could do was wait

337
00:19:20,218 --> 00:19:23,681
and keep training in the hopes
of being able to participate.

338
00:19:23,691 --> 00:19:27,181
So I kept running and checked off
more slots in my training plan,

339
00:19:27,191 --> 00:19:30,006
but in my fifth run of 30 kilometers,

340
00:19:30,016 --> 00:19:34,536
I injured my leg and had to
stop after only 5 kilometers.

341
00:19:34,546 --> 00:19:37,364
My right leg is just starting to hurt...

342
00:19:37,735 --> 00:19:38,678
a lot.

343
00:19:38,688 --> 00:19:40,295
Just this lower part here,

344
00:19:40,595 --> 00:19:41,849
and the calves.

345
00:19:41,859 --> 00:19:44,737
I don't know why I'm feeling very weak today,

346
00:19:44,747 --> 00:19:47,555
and even like 5 kilometers, I'm struggling.

347
00:19:47,565 --> 00:19:48,870
This sucks, man.

348
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:51,859
It's all kind of crumbling down at the moment.

349
00:19:53,787 --> 00:19:56,099
I'm actually doubting myself right now

350
00:19:56,109 --> 00:19:59,137
if I'll be able to run 42 kilometers or if...

351
00:19:59,657 --> 00:20:01,925
this goal was just way too huge for me.

352
00:20:01,935 --> 00:20:04,399
Also, update on the ticket situation.

353
00:20:04,409 --> 00:20:08,437
I haven't heard back from them in 4 days
now since I've sent out that email,

354
00:20:08,447 --> 00:20:10,134
so I guess right now

355
00:20:10,144 --> 00:20:13,215
I'm just training with a hurting leg

356
00:20:13,409 --> 00:20:16,214
for a marathon I don't have a ticket for.

357
00:20:17,064 --> 00:20:18,008
F*ck.

358
00:20:18,317 --> 00:20:21,805
This was the first run that I
couldn't finish because of pain,

359
00:20:21,815 --> 00:20:23,891
and my motivation was drained.

360
00:20:23,901 --> 00:20:28,731
Still, after one day of resting, I decided
to give the 30k a second try.

361
00:20:28,741 --> 00:20:30,765
I properly warmed myself up,

362
00:20:30,775 --> 00:20:32,920
started the watch and began to run.

363
00:20:32,930 --> 00:20:35,859
The first few minutes, everything
felt like it was going well,

364
00:20:35,869 --> 00:20:38,593
but at kilometer 3, things changed.

365
00:20:38,603 --> 00:20:43,255
I'm only 3 kilometers in, and I can
already feel my right calf is not good.

366
00:20:43,265 --> 00:20:46,593
After quickly checking my calf,
I decided to keep going,

367
00:20:46,603 --> 00:20:49,912
but the more I ran, the stronger the pain became.

368
00:20:50,924 --> 00:20:53,142
My calf is just hurting so much.

369
00:20:53,152 --> 00:20:56,884
It feels like somebody's just stabbing with
a knife into it all the time when I run.

370
00:20:56,894 --> 00:20:58,516
Where is this coming from, hey?

371
00:20:59,332 --> 00:21:03,140
I think I'm going to try to keep going
until I just can't anymore.

372
00:21:03,150 --> 00:21:04,905
This is my last chance, hey.

373
00:21:04,915 --> 00:21:05,745
F*ck.

374
00:21:05,755 --> 00:21:08,355
I tried to get rid of the pain
by massaging my leg,

375
00:21:08,365 --> 00:21:10,518
but after a few more minutes of running,

376
00:21:10,528 --> 00:21:13,887
I had to realize that this was not going to work.

377
00:21:13,897 --> 00:21:14,894
F*ck!

378
00:21:16,288 --> 00:21:18,997
I think it would be absolutely
stupid to just keep going,

379
00:21:19,007 --> 00:21:20,340
to see it get worse.

380
00:21:20,350 --> 00:21:24,874
It's just that I don't have any training in
these last like one or two weeks.

381
00:21:24,884 --> 00:21:27,588
I was forced to give up and walked back home,

382
00:21:27,598 --> 00:21:30,238
as there was simply no chance to keep running.

383
00:21:30,553 --> 00:21:35,099
So after doing some research on the Internet
about the pain that I'm experiencing right now,

384
00:21:35,109 --> 00:21:39,858
I just found out that I most likely
have a rupture in a muscle fiber,

385
00:21:39,868 --> 00:21:43,621
and they say that it can take
3 to 12 weeks in order to heal.

386
00:21:43,631 --> 00:21:46,025
But as you know, my marathon is in 2 weeks,

387
00:21:46,035 --> 00:21:47,372
so...

388
00:21:47,382 --> 00:21:49,170
it freaking looks like...

389
00:21:49,733 --> 00:21:51,581
I'm not going to run a marathon.

390
00:21:53,915 --> 00:21:55,261
I was devastated.

391
00:21:55,271 --> 00:21:58,221
Were all of my efforts of the
last 6 weeks for nothing?

392
00:21:58,231 --> 00:21:59,865
All the time spent preparing,

393
00:21:59,875 --> 00:22:03,761
all the hours spent running and all the
painful stretching sessions in between,

394
00:22:03,771 --> 00:22:06,298
all the tears and sweats for nothing?

395
00:22:06,308 --> 00:22:09,234
I had dedicated my whole life
to this huge goal of mine,

396
00:22:09,244 --> 00:22:12,677
and now my dream of running
a marathon vanished into air.

397
00:22:12,687 --> 00:22:16,758
My longest run so far was 28 kilometers,
and because of my injury,

398
00:22:16,768 --> 00:22:20,965
I wasn't able to do a single run within
the last two weeks of my training.

399
00:22:20,975 --> 00:22:23,140
I had given up all my hopes.

400
00:22:24,588 --> 00:22:29,185
On my flight to Cape Town, I had very
mixed feelings about arriving to South Africa.

401
00:22:29,195 --> 00:22:31,829
I was excited to finally move
to another continent,

402
00:22:31,839 --> 00:22:36,422
but at the same time, I slowly
realized that I had failed.

403
00:22:36,432 --> 00:22:38,119
I checked into my apartment,

404
00:22:38,129 --> 00:22:40,905
and after reflecting on what I had gone through,

405
00:22:40,915 --> 00:22:43,719
I simply couldn't end it like this.

406
00:22:43,729 --> 00:22:46,674
It is one more week until
the marathon takes place

407
00:22:46,684 --> 00:22:49,415
and I thought "I'm gonna
give this one last chance".

408
00:22:49,425 --> 00:22:51,392
I'm gonna go for a 10k run

409
00:22:51,402 --> 00:22:53,751
and I'm gonna see if the pain is still there.

410
00:22:53,761 --> 00:22:56,079
I tried to recover for the last couple of days,

411
00:22:56,089 --> 00:22:58,096
and I hope that it was worth it.

412
00:22:58,106 --> 00:23:01,081
Just wish me luck that the pain disappeared.

413
00:23:29,039 --> 00:23:31,286
So, I've now been running 8 kilometers,

414
00:23:31,296 --> 00:23:35,683
and my calves are feeling really good.
No pain anymore, so that's great news.

415
00:23:35,693 --> 00:23:38,365
I just decided that I'm gonna run it, f*ck it.

416
00:23:38,375 --> 00:23:40,927
I'm gonna run it and I'm gonna see how far I get.

417
00:23:40,937 --> 00:23:42,139
Let's do this!

418
00:23:43,342 --> 00:23:44,821
I was back on track.

419
00:23:44,831 --> 00:23:47,115
Even though I only ran a short distance,

420
00:23:47,125 --> 00:23:51,474
I gained back a lot of confidence as there
was no sign of my pain in my leg.

421
00:23:53,041 --> 00:23:54,045
Hey.

422
00:23:54,398 --> 00:23:56,042
The first fans arrived.

423
00:23:56,892 --> 00:23:59,177
And as if the whole universe aligned,

424
00:23:59,187 --> 00:24:01,239
five days before the marathon,

425
00:24:01,249 --> 00:24:03,539
I heard back from the racing committee.

426
00:24:03,549 --> 00:24:08,447
Yo guys, you won't believe what email
e-mail I just received. Look at this.

427
00:24:08,457 --> 00:24:11,698
I just got my marathon ticket.

428
00:24:11,708 --> 00:24:14,405
I really didn't expect that anymore.

429
00:24:14,415 --> 00:24:17,112
I can't freaking wait to run that marathon.

430
00:25:00,610 --> 00:25:04,365
So, everybody's just checking into the
different starting blocks right now.

431
00:25:04,375 --> 00:25:08,624
It's just getting very real for me right now
that I'm going to run for 42 kilometers.

432
00:25:08,634 --> 00:25:09,981
I'm feeling good so far.

433
00:25:09,991 --> 00:25:12,781
I've been training for this moment
for the last 2 months,

434
00:25:12,791 --> 00:25:15,893
and it's just like a lot of tension around here.

435
00:25:15,903 --> 00:25:19,231
All of the people are back here
just like building up.

436
00:25:23,541 --> 00:25:25,057
I love that mood.

437
00:25:26,593 --> 00:25:28,808
We're entering the starting block right now.

438
00:25:32,360 --> 00:25:33,277
F*ck.

439
00:25:33,287 --> 00:25:34,337
This is happening.

440
00:25:34,347 --> 00:25:35,439
Have fun!

441
00:25:35,449 --> 00:25:37,268
Make wise choices.

442
00:25:38,627 --> 00:25:42,166
And there I was, waiting for
the countdown to start.

443
00:25:42,176 --> 00:25:43,029
8,

444
00:25:43,039 --> 00:25:43,919
7,

445
00:25:43,929 --> 00:25:45,034
6,

446
00:25:45,044 --> 00:25:45,927
5,

447
00:25:45,937 --> 00:25:46,766
4,

448
00:25:47,064 --> 00:25:47,892
3,

449
00:25:47,902 --> 00:25:48,785
2,

450
00:25:48,795 --> 00:25:49,492
1!

451
00:25:51,721 --> 00:25:52,879
Let's do this!

452
00:25:57,787 --> 00:25:58,858
I love the energy.

453
00:25:58,868 --> 00:26:00,933
Guys, that's how you do it. Yes!

454
00:26:00,943 --> 00:26:04,398
I'm just kind of trying to get into a zone,
listening to some techno music

455
00:26:04,408 --> 00:26:06,229
for the like first 10 kilometers.

456
00:26:14,019 --> 00:26:15,045
Let's go!

457
00:26:15,465 --> 00:26:17,947
So, I'm now at 10 kilometers,
so far it's feeling well.

458
00:26:18,768 --> 00:26:20,842
There's a lot of energy here for sure.

459
00:26:20,852 --> 00:26:23,235
I can definitely slowly feel my muscles.

460
00:26:28,539 --> 00:26:30,842
The one with the flag, that's a pacemaker.

461
00:26:30,852 --> 00:26:33,172
It's basically one guy trying to keep up

462
00:26:33,182 --> 00:26:36,395
the exact same pace so that the others
know how fast they are.

463
00:26:38,019 --> 00:26:39,626
Yo, let's do it!

464
00:26:39,926 --> 00:26:41,889
Everything was going as planned so far,

465
00:26:41,899 --> 00:26:45,618
but obviously there was one thing
that needed to happen.

466
00:26:49,134 --> 00:26:50,348
And back we are,

467
00:26:50,358 --> 00:26:52,345
to the long runs in the rain.

468
00:26:53,206 --> 00:26:54,695
What the f*ck is this.

469
00:26:58,392 --> 00:27:01,381
It looks like my many long runs
in the rain finally paid off,

470
00:27:01,391 --> 00:27:03,544
as I was used to running with wet feet.

471
00:27:03,554 --> 00:27:05,852
I kept up the spirit and pushed through the rain.

472
00:27:05,862 --> 00:27:08,641
After one hour, the weather finally
started to get better again,

473
00:27:08,651 --> 00:27:11,131
but I couldn't say the same for my energy.

474
00:27:11,141 --> 00:27:13,391
So I'm now at 21k, half time.

475
00:27:13,401 --> 00:27:15,704
I can definitely feel that
I'm getting weaker now.

476
00:27:15,714 --> 00:27:17,115
I'm getting a little lightheaded.

477
00:27:17,125 --> 00:27:19,242
I have to eat some sort of sugar...

478
00:27:19,454 --> 00:27:20,444
in the next minute.

479
00:27:20,454 --> 00:27:21,877
I decided to eat my POWERGEL,

480
00:27:21,887 --> 00:27:25,595
and within only a few minutes, I could
already feel my energy coming back.

481
00:27:25,885 --> 00:27:27,290
That is the best thing

482
00:27:27,615 --> 00:27:28,738
I've ever eaten.

483
00:27:29,183 --> 00:27:30,392
This feels so good.

484
00:27:30,660 --> 00:27:31,740
Definitely gives me a boost.

485
00:27:31,750 --> 00:27:34,728
So as you might remember,
my brother ran a time of 3:41,

486
00:27:34,738 --> 00:27:37,432
so my goal for this marathon
is not just to finish it,

487
00:27:37,442 --> 00:27:38,896
but actually to beat my brother.

488
00:27:38,906 --> 00:27:42,421
He deserves it. He's always been talking
about it for the last two years.

489
00:27:42,431 --> 00:27:45,301
That's just a brother thing, I have to beat him.

490
00:27:48,391 --> 00:27:51,061
The goal to beat my brother
fueled my motivation even more

491
00:27:51,071 --> 00:27:53,510
and made me push harder with each kilometer.

492
00:27:53,951 --> 00:27:57,171
I was amazed by how many people
showed up to support the runners.

493
00:27:57,181 --> 00:27:58,876
Holy shit, so many people out here.

494
00:27:59,158 --> 00:28:01,443
There were literally hundreds of people cheering,

495
00:28:01,453 --> 00:28:05,567
playing drums or handing out high fives
in order to help us get through this marathon.

496
00:28:05,577 --> 00:28:07,108
Let's go, Niklas!

497
00:28:07,118 --> 00:28:08,688
Let's go, Niklas!

498
00:28:08,698 --> 00:28:10,233
Let's go, Niklas!

499
00:28:10,243 --> 00:28:11,787
Let's go, Niklas!

500
00:28:11,797 --> 00:28:13,120
Let's go, Niklas!

501
00:28:13,130 --> 00:28:14,885
Let's go, Niklas!

502
00:28:14,895 --> 00:28:16,721
Let's go, Niklas!

503
00:28:16,731 --> 00:28:19,051
Let's go, Niklas!

504
00:28:19,061 --> 00:28:20,570
Come on, keep going!

505
00:28:22,415 --> 00:28:26,024
The energy of this whole event was
something I've never experienced before.

506
00:28:26,034 --> 00:28:29,621
The fact that thousands of strangers were
going through the same challenge right now

507
00:28:29,631 --> 00:28:32,114
made me believe that together we can do it.

508
00:28:32,124 --> 00:28:33,647
Hey, my man. How's the music?

509
00:28:35,479 --> 00:28:37,291
- How is it going?
- Totally fine.

510
00:28:37,301 --> 00:28:38,548
Tunisians are strong.

511
00:28:38,558 --> 00:28:39,805
Perfect, good luck man.

512
00:28:39,815 --> 00:28:40,621
You too.

513
00:28:41,074 --> 00:28:44,450
More than two hours into the marathon,
I now approached the 30k mark,

514
00:28:44,460 --> 00:28:47,155
which was more than the maximum
distance of my training.

515
00:28:47,165 --> 00:28:49,946
From now on, I was in uncharted territory.

516
00:28:50,643 --> 00:28:53,714
32 kilometers, my body is f*cking killing me.

517
00:28:53,724 --> 00:28:55,510
I can feel my legs everywhere,

518
00:28:55,520 --> 00:28:57,692
and I'm feeling a bit light-headed.

519
00:28:57,702 --> 00:28:59,113
I have to keep up the pace.

520
00:28:59,316 --> 00:29:00,596
I can't slow down.

521
00:29:02,865 --> 00:29:05,035
This was when the hardest part started.

522
00:29:05,045 --> 00:29:10,262
If I wanted to beat my brother, I would need to
keep up the same pace for the last 10 kilometers.

523
00:29:14,203 --> 00:29:15,589
I feel like I need more sugar.

524
00:29:15,599 --> 00:29:19,031
I tried refueling my energy by eating
sweets and drinking soft drinks,

525
00:29:19,041 --> 00:29:22,757
but I couldn't ignore the fact that
my body was slowly shutting off.

526
00:29:22,767 --> 00:29:24,477
Oh my God, my legs are shutting down.

527
00:29:24,487 --> 00:29:26,129
Still 9 kilometers to go.

528
00:29:28,239 --> 00:29:30,172
This is getting so f*cking hard right now.

529
00:29:31,240 --> 00:29:32,519
And it's uphill.

530
00:29:32,529 --> 00:29:34,276
For the last 5 kilometers,

531
00:29:34,286 --> 00:29:35,910
I've been struggling really hard.

532
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:38,303
I'm not quite sure if I can keep up the pace.

533
00:29:38,313 --> 00:29:40,686
It's like everything is just hurting.

534
00:29:40,696 --> 00:29:42,011
You got this.

535
00:29:43,070 --> 00:29:46,565
From this point on, it was all up
to my own willpower.

536
00:29:46,575 --> 00:29:50,037
After running for 39 kilometers,
my lower body was covered in pain

537
00:29:50,047 --> 00:29:51,750
and I could barely feel my legs.

538
00:29:51,760 --> 00:29:53,469
My legs are hurting so bad.

539
00:29:54,241 --> 00:29:59,181
I tried motivating myself over and over
again to not give up and finish this run.

540
00:30:00,541 --> 00:30:02,452
The last kilometer, almost there.

541
00:30:02,462 --> 00:30:04,650
I can f*cking do it. Come on, let's go!

542
00:30:04,660 --> 00:30:08,769
There it was, the moment I dedicated
my life to for the last months.

543
00:30:08,779 --> 00:30:11,122
I finally made the decision to run a marathon

544
00:30:11,132 --> 00:30:13,623
and bought all the necessary
equipment to get started.

545
00:30:13,633 --> 00:30:17,178
I headed out day and night to
run and improve my physical strength.

546
00:30:17,188 --> 00:30:21,330
I researched about my weaknesses and did
anything needed to keep my muscles strong

547
00:30:21,340 --> 00:30:22,577
and my joints healthy.

548
00:30:22,587 --> 00:30:26,698
No matter what mood I was in, I sticked to the
training plan and showed up for the runs.

549
00:30:26,708 --> 00:30:27,891
Let's do it!

550
00:30:34,712 --> 00:30:37,820
Sore muscles, pouring rain, painful stretches.

551
00:30:37,830 --> 00:30:40,269
None of those things counted as an excuse.

552
00:30:40,279 --> 00:30:42,205
You might ask yourself "why run?

553
00:30:42,215 --> 00:30:43,620
Why do this to yourself?

554
00:30:43,630 --> 00:30:47,186
Why push yourself until your muscles
give up and you can't breathe?".

555
00:30:47,196 --> 00:30:49,337
I used to ask the same questions back then,

556
00:30:49,347 --> 00:30:53,876
but during the marathon, I started to realize
what this whole journey was about.

557
00:30:53,886 --> 00:30:55,984
When you're running, it's you against you.

558
00:30:55,994 --> 00:30:58,947
No players, no competitors, no enemies.

559
00:30:58,957 --> 00:31:01,664
It's you against your own body and your mind.

560
00:31:01,674 --> 00:31:03,622
Foot after foot, breath after breath,

561
00:31:03,632 --> 00:31:06,176
you push yourself to go further, go faster.

562
00:31:06,186 --> 00:31:08,745
You can feel your body sweating
and your heart pumping.

563
00:31:08,755 --> 00:31:11,115
Mile after mile, you push yourself to not give up.

564
00:31:11,125 --> 00:31:13,559
Your muscles get weak, your feet start hurting,

565
00:31:13,569 --> 00:31:15,977
and your body is telling you to stop.

566
00:31:17,316 --> 00:31:18,886
But you still keep going.

567
00:31:18,896 --> 00:31:20,923
Running is the essence of ambition.

568
00:31:20,933 --> 00:31:23,935
Always fighting, always pushing,
always improving.

569
00:31:23,945 --> 00:31:27,599
It's about embracing the discomfort
and breaking your mental barriers.

570
00:31:27,609 --> 00:31:30,047
You realize that with dedication and hard work

571
00:31:30,057 --> 00:31:31,771
your body can do anything,

572
00:31:31,781 --> 00:31:33,148
and so can your mind.

573
00:31:33,158 --> 00:31:36,257
Would I've believed that I could run
a marathon three years ago?

574
00:31:36,267 --> 00:31:40,079
Would I've believed that I could make a living
from creating these YouTube videos?

575
00:31:40,089 --> 00:31:43,881
Would I have believed that I'd be able
to live on the other side of this planet?

576
00:31:43,891 --> 00:31:45,216
No, I wouldn't have.

577
00:31:45,226 --> 00:31:47,845
Running taught me the most
important lesson in life.

578
00:31:47,855 --> 00:31:51,608
It taught that we're aware of only a fraction
of the things we're capable of,

579
00:31:51,618 --> 00:31:55,095
and that our limitations only exist in our minds.

580
00:31:55,649 --> 00:31:56,886
Let's go!

581
00:32:01,758 --> 00:32:02,931
That's it.

582
00:32:02,941 --> 00:32:04,673
There's the finish line.

583
00:32:11,418 --> 00:32:13,359
Record-breaking her very first marathon.

584
00:32:14,016 --> 00:32:16,398
She comes over to the land.

585
00:32:16,715 --> 00:32:18,334
From Kenya to South Africa.

586
00:32:18,344 --> 00:32:19,743
What a beautiful race.

587
00:32:19,753 --> 00:32:20,782
What a beautiful race.

588
00:32:20,792 --> 00:32:23,029
The most beautiful beautiful ever.

589
00:32:23,039 --> 00:32:24,482
I loved it, man.

590
00:32:24,492 --> 00:32:25,794
Holy shit.

591
00:32:34,141 --> 00:32:35,830
There it is, guys. There it is.

592
00:32:35,840 --> 00:32:37,368
I f*cking did it.

593
00:32:37,378 --> 00:32:41,364
And according to my Apple Watch,
I did a time of 3:34,

594
00:32:41,374 --> 00:32:44,297
which means that I f*cking beat my brother.

595
00:32:44,307 --> 00:32:45,835
Take that, Max!

596
00:32:46,470 --> 00:32:47,439
Wow.

597
00:32:47,449 --> 00:32:48,310
Wow.

598
00:32:48,320 --> 00:32:50,821
This was freaking crazy, oh my God.

599
00:32:55,343 --> 00:32:56,548
Let's call him.

600
00:32:59,506 --> 00:33:00,495
Hey Max.

601
00:33:01,738 --> 00:33:02,953
Look at that.

602
00:33:03,722 --> 00:33:05,045
Guess what time I did?

603
00:33:05,271 --> 00:33:06,702
I already know it.

604
00:33:08,261 --> 00:33:09,563
Tell me, tell me.

605
00:33:10,015 --> 00:33:11,873
A little bit less than mine.

606
00:33:12,688 --> 00:33:14,433
3:34, boy.

607
00:33:16,267 --> 00:33:18,219
Honestly, well done, well done Niklas.

608
00:33:18,229 --> 00:33:20,376
Thanks man. You know what that means.

609
00:33:20,386 --> 00:33:22,613
You have to run a marathon again.

610
00:33:22,974 --> 00:33:25,678
- I don't know about that.
- I know about it.

611
00:33:25,688 --> 00:33:28,726
I'm just so happy that I finished this marathon.

612
00:33:28,736 --> 00:33:33,108
This just showed me once again that
the limits are much higher than you think,

613
00:33:33,118 --> 00:33:36,608
and this is I think the main takeaway
that I want to give to you guys,

614
00:33:36,618 --> 00:33:39,613
that if you have any sort of dream,
then you can just realize it

615
00:33:39,623 --> 00:33:42,397
and you can do it, even if
there are people doubting you.

616
00:33:42,407 --> 00:33:45,774
You just have to believe in yourself,
you have to dedicate the time to do it,

617
00:33:45,784 --> 00:33:47,221
and then you can make it happen.

618
00:33:47,231 --> 00:33:48,580
That's it for today, guys.

619
00:33:48,590 --> 00:33:50,546
I'm going to see you in the next one.

620
00:33:50,556 --> 00:33:52,474
Peace out, bye bye.

